1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,632
Sweetheart, on Christmas Eve of two thousand

2
00:00:03,632 --> 00:00:06,604
sixteen, my own family drove off and

3
00:00:06,604 --> 00:00:08,833
left me at a gas station in

4
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:10,650
the middle of Indiana,

5
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:11,888
in a snowstorm,

6
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:12,961
with no coat,

7
00:00:12,961 --> 00:00:14,860
no phone, and no purse.

8
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,412
Nobody noticed I was gone for a

9
00:00:17,412 --> 00:00:19,324
hundred and twelve miles.

10
00:00:19,504 --> 00:00:21,615
And the man who found me crying

11
00:00:21,615 --> 00:00:23,793
by the ice machine was a trucker

12
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:26,380
named Jerome, who was spending his own

13
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:27,469
Christmas alone.

14
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,947
Tonight I'm going to tell you how

15
00:00:29,947 --> 00:00:32,139
it happened, what Jerome did for a

16
00:00:32,139 --> 00:00:33,429
stranger that night,

17
00:00:33,429 --> 00:00:35,364
and the phone call my son made

18
00:00:35,364 --> 00:00:37,815
at ten o'clock that I'll never forget.

19
00:00:37,995 --> 00:00:38,970
Stay with me,

20
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:41,895
honey, because the ending of this story

21
00:00:41,895 --> 00:00:44,220
is the reason I now spend every

22
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,470
Christmas Eve at a truck stop.

23
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:49,529
And I wouldn't trade it for anything.

24
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,962
That year, my son Mark and his

25
00:00:51,962 --> 00:00:54,391
wife invited me to Christmas at her

26
00:00:54,391 --> 00:00:56,265
parents' house in Illinois.

27
00:00:56,445 --> 00:00:58,233
Seven hours in the car.

28
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:00,023
Mark, his wife Jenna,

29
00:01:00,023 --> 00:01:01,710
their three teenagers,

30
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:04,087
and me, squeezed in the back of

31
00:01:04,087 --> 00:01:07,000
the minivan between a pile of presents

32
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,220
and a sixteen-year-old with headphones on.

33
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,863
I was seventy-two.

34
00:01:12,043 --> 00:01:13,703
My knees didn't love it.

35
00:01:13,883 --> 00:01:15,985
But I was happy to be wanted.

36
00:01:16,335 --> 00:01:18,452
Now, my family loves me,

37
00:01:18,452 --> 00:01:19,423
sweetheart.

38
00:01:19,603 --> 00:01:21,571
I want you to know that before

39
00:01:21,571 --> 00:01:22,621
I tell the rest.

40
00:01:22,801 --> 00:01:24,404
But they're busy people.

41
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:26,592
Everybody's on a phone.

42
00:01:26,772 --> 00:01:28,688
Everybody's in a hurry.

43
00:01:28,868 --> 00:01:31,336
Jenna had a schedule printed out,

44
00:01:31,336 --> 00:01:33,430
with exactly when we'd stop.

45
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:34,851
And I'd noticed,

46
00:01:34,851 --> 00:01:36,324
the last few years,

47
00:01:36,324 --> 00:01:39,038
that I'd started to become a little

48
00:01:39,038 --> 00:01:40,124
bit invisible.

49
00:01:40,304 --> 00:01:42,697
A quiet old lady in the back

50
00:01:42,697 --> 00:01:43,125
seat.

51
00:01:43,305 --> 00:01:45,282
In a minute I'll tell you how

52
00:01:45,282 --> 00:01:45,964
invisible.

53
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:48,167
Around four o'clock,

54
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:49,929
in western Indiana,

55
00:01:49,929 --> 00:01:52,153
it started to snow hard.

56
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:54,820
Mark pulled off at a big truck

57
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:57,639
stop for gas and a bathroom break.

58
00:01:57,819 --> 00:02:00,095
Ten minutes, Jenna said.

59
00:02:00,275 --> 00:02:03,200
Everybody back in ten minutes.

60
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:04,594
I took my time,

61
00:02:04,594 --> 00:02:07,426
honey, because my knees were stiff,

62
00:02:07,426 --> 00:02:09,691
and there was a long line at

63
00:02:09,691 --> 00:02:11,066
the ladies' room.

64
00:02:11,246 --> 00:02:13,294
I left my coat and purse in

65
00:02:13,294 --> 00:02:15,568
the van, because I'd only be a

66
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:16,099
minute.

67
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:19,174
When I came out of that bathroom,

68
00:02:19,174 --> 00:02:20,908
the minivan was gone.

69
00:02:21,088 --> 00:02:23,272
I stood there in the doorway in

70
00:02:23,272 --> 00:02:26,019
my cardigan, looking at the empty pump,

71
00:02:26,019 --> 00:02:28,344
and at first I didn't understand.

72
00:02:28,524 --> 00:02:30,873
I thought maybe they'd moved to a

73
00:02:30,873 --> 00:02:31,798
parking spot.

74
00:02:31,978 --> 00:02:34,214
I walked up and down the lot

75
00:02:34,214 --> 00:02:35,172
in the snow,

76
00:02:35,172 --> 00:02:36,529
in my good shoes,

77
00:02:36,529 --> 00:02:37,168
looking.

78
00:02:37,348 --> 00:02:38,602
No minivan.

79
00:02:38,782 --> 00:02:40,964
They had driven off without me.

80
00:02:41,144 --> 00:02:42,491
My own son.

81
00:02:42,841 --> 00:02:45,406
Later I found out how it happened.

82
00:02:45,586 --> 00:02:47,806
Jenna thought I was in the very

83
00:02:47,806 --> 00:02:49,667
back row, under the coats,

84
00:02:49,667 --> 00:02:50,312
sleeping.

85
00:02:50,492 --> 00:02:52,965
The kids had their headphones on.

86
00:02:53,145 --> 00:02:55,593
Mark counted heads in the mirror and

87
00:02:55,593 --> 00:02:57,701
saw a lump of coats and thought

88
00:02:57,701 --> 00:02:58,381
it was me.

89
00:02:58,561 --> 00:03:00,125
And off they went,

90
00:03:00,125 --> 00:03:01,950
honey, into the snow,

91
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:05,427
toward Illinois, a hundred miles an hour

92
00:03:05,427 --> 00:03:08,209
of busy, and nobody looked back.

93
00:03:08,559 --> 00:03:10,172
I had no phone.

94
00:03:10,352 --> 00:03:12,739
I'm seventy-two, sweetheart,

95
00:03:12,739 --> 00:03:15,127
and I'd left it in my purse,

96
00:03:15,127 --> 00:03:16,064
in the van.

97
00:03:16,244 --> 00:03:18,676
I didn't know my son's cell phone

98
00:03:18,676 --> 00:03:19,855
number by heart.

99
00:03:20,035 --> 00:03:21,394
Who does anymore?

100
00:03:21,574 --> 00:03:24,348
I didn't know Jenna's parents' address.

101
00:03:24,528 --> 00:03:27,028
I had four dollars in my cardigan

102
00:03:27,028 --> 00:03:27,559
pocket.

103
00:03:27,739 --> 00:03:29,424
And it was getting dark,

104
00:03:29,424 --> 00:03:31,742
and the snow was coming sideways,

105
00:03:31,742 --> 00:03:33,850
and every car pulling in was a

106
00:03:33,850 --> 00:03:36,098
family going home for Christmas.

107
00:03:36,448 --> 00:03:39,220
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

108
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:41,359
tap the like button for me,

109
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:41,835
honey.

110
00:03:42,015 --> 00:03:45,312
It helps more people find these stories.

111
00:03:45,492 --> 00:03:47,494
I went inside and sat down on

112
00:03:47,494 --> 00:03:49,772
a little bench by the ice machine

113
00:03:49,772 --> 00:03:50,738
near the door,

114
00:03:50,738 --> 00:03:52,809
so I'd see them when they came

115
00:03:52,809 --> 00:03:53,154
back.

116
00:03:53,334 --> 00:03:54,577
And I waited.

117
00:03:54,757 --> 00:03:56,034
Thirty minutes.

118
00:03:56,214 --> 00:03:57,084
An hour.

119
00:03:57,264 --> 00:03:58,878
They didn't come back.

120
00:03:59,058 --> 00:04:01,831
And somewhere in that second hour,

121
00:04:01,831 --> 00:04:04,115
sitting by that ice machine,

122
00:04:04,115 --> 00:04:05,502
I started to cry.

123
00:04:05,852 --> 00:04:08,208
Not loud, sweetheart.

124
00:04:08,388 --> 00:04:10,160
Just tears running down,

125
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,448
the way they do when you're old

126
00:04:12,448 --> 00:04:15,622
and tired and you've been feeling invisible

127
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:16,803
for a long time,

128
00:04:16,803 --> 00:04:18,501
and now you really are.

129
00:04:18,681 --> 00:04:20,991
People walked right past me.

130
00:04:21,171 --> 00:04:22,801
A hundred people,

131
00:04:22,801 --> 00:04:23,377
maybe.

132
00:04:23,557 --> 00:04:26,065
Families with shopping bags.

133
00:04:26,245 --> 00:04:27,371
Teenagers.

134
00:04:27,551 --> 00:04:29,631
A man in a suit on his

135
00:04:29,631 --> 00:04:30,198
phone.

136
00:04:30,378 --> 00:04:31,632
Nobody stopped.

137
00:04:31,812 --> 00:04:33,672
And then a big pair of work

138
00:04:33,672 --> 00:04:36,084
boots stopped right in front of me.

139
00:04:36,435 --> 00:04:37,786
He was a big man,

140
00:04:37,786 --> 00:04:39,297
honey, maybe sixty,

141
00:04:39,297 --> 00:04:41,763
with a gray beard and a flannel

142
00:04:41,763 --> 00:04:44,228
shirt and a cap that said Jesus

143
00:04:44,228 --> 00:04:45,421
Loves Truckers.

144
00:04:45,601 --> 00:04:46,962
He said, ma'am,

145
00:04:46,962 --> 00:04:48,596
are you all right?

146
00:04:48,776 --> 00:04:50,808
Are you waiting for somebody?

147
00:04:50,988 --> 00:04:51,868
And I said,

148
00:04:51,868 --> 00:04:53,948
I'm waiting for my family.

149
00:04:54,128 --> 00:04:55,347
They left me.

150
00:04:55,527 --> 00:04:57,620
And I heard how it sounded out

151
00:04:57,620 --> 00:05:00,062
loud, and I started crying all over

152
00:05:00,062 --> 00:05:02,784
again, right in front of that stranger.

153
00:05:03,134 --> 00:05:05,049
His name was Jerome.

154
00:05:05,229 --> 00:05:07,402
He sat down on that bench next

155
00:05:07,402 --> 00:05:09,502
to me, which took some doing,

156
00:05:09,502 --> 00:05:11,531
because he was a big man and

157
00:05:11,531 --> 00:05:13,124
it was a little bench.

158
00:05:13,304 --> 00:05:14,322
And he said,

159
00:05:14,322 --> 00:05:17,632
well, ma'am, I reckon they'll figure it

160
00:05:17,632 --> 00:05:19,074
out pretty quick.

161
00:05:19,254 --> 00:05:21,379
Meantime, you're freezing.

162
00:05:21,559 --> 00:05:23,622
And he went out to his truck

163
00:05:23,622 --> 00:05:25,759
and came back with a big wool

164
00:05:25,759 --> 00:05:28,265
jacket that came down to my knees,

165
00:05:28,265 --> 00:05:30,255
and a cup of hot chocolate.

166
00:05:30,605 --> 00:05:33,175
Then he asked the right questions,

167
00:05:33,175 --> 00:05:34,006
sweetheart.

168
00:05:34,186 --> 00:05:35,881
What's your son's name?

169
00:05:36,061 --> 00:05:37,814
Where does he live?

170
00:05:37,994 --> 00:05:39,422
What kind of car?

171
00:05:39,602 --> 00:05:42,145
Do you know his wife's last name?

172
00:05:42,325 --> 00:05:44,008
Her parents' town?

173
00:05:44,188 --> 00:05:45,686
I knew the town.

174
00:05:45,866 --> 00:05:46,853
Peoria.

175
00:05:47,033 --> 00:05:49,417
And Jerome took out his phone and

176
00:05:49,417 --> 00:05:50,934
started making calls.

177
00:05:51,114 --> 00:05:53,982
The Illinois Highway Patrol.

178
00:05:54,162 --> 00:05:56,542
The Indiana State Police.

179
00:05:56,722 --> 00:05:59,390
Two trucker friends who were driving west

180
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:00,692
on the same highway.

181
00:06:01,043 --> 00:06:03,131
He got on his CB radio,

182
00:06:03,131 --> 00:06:05,129
too, out in his truck.

183
00:06:05,309 --> 00:06:07,775
He told every trucker on that highway

184
00:06:07,775 --> 00:06:09,840
to look for a blue minivan with

185
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:12,306
Ohio plates and a Christmas wreath on

186
00:06:12,306 --> 00:06:12,972
the grill.

187
00:06:13,152 --> 00:06:14,698
And for the next hour,

188
00:06:14,698 --> 00:06:17,440
honey, I could hear the radio crackling

189
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,549
through his open truck window.

190
00:06:19,729 --> 00:06:21,659
Truckers from all over,

191
00:06:21,659 --> 00:06:22,666
checking in.

192
00:06:22,846 --> 00:06:23,473
Nope.

193
00:06:23,653 --> 00:06:24,686
Not yet.

194
00:06:24,866 --> 00:06:25,935
Keep looking.

195
00:06:26,115 --> 00:06:29,284
Nobody's leaving grandma at a truck stop

196
00:06:29,284 --> 00:06:30,631
on Christmas Eve.

197
00:06:30,981 --> 00:06:32,645
So far, the van,

198
00:06:32,645 --> 00:06:35,455
the coats, the ice machine,

199
00:06:35,455 --> 00:06:36,600
and Jerome.

200
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:37,928
While we waited,

201
00:06:37,928 --> 00:06:40,728
Jerome bought us two plates of meatloaf

202
00:06:40,728 --> 00:06:41,661
in the diner,

203
00:06:41,661 --> 00:06:42,666
and we talked.

204
00:06:42,846 --> 00:06:45,062
I asked him where he was going

205
00:06:45,062 --> 00:06:46,097
for Christmas.

206
00:06:46,277 --> 00:06:47,766
And he got quiet,

207
00:06:47,766 --> 00:06:48,817
and he said,

208
00:06:48,817 --> 00:06:50,131
nowhere, ma'am.

209
00:06:50,311 --> 00:06:52,628
He was spending Christmas Eve in the

210
00:06:52,628 --> 00:06:54,108
truck stop parking lot.

211
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:56,385
Like he had for the last four

212
00:06:56,385 --> 00:06:56,819
years.

213
00:06:57,169 --> 00:06:58,825
His wife, Loretta,

214
00:06:58,825 --> 00:07:01,310
had died four years before,

215
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:02,230
of cancer.

216
00:07:02,410 --> 00:07:05,104
They'd been married thirty-one years.

217
00:07:05,284 --> 00:07:06,677
They had one daughter,

218
00:07:06,677 --> 00:07:09,147
and she'd stopped speaking to him after

219
00:07:09,147 --> 00:07:11,681
the funeral, over something he'd said in

220
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,771
grief that he couldn't take back.

221
00:07:13,951 --> 00:07:16,535
He'd been on the road ever since,

222
00:07:16,535 --> 00:07:17,004
honey.

223
00:07:17,184 --> 00:07:19,909
He said, it's easier to drive than

224
00:07:19,909 --> 00:07:22,072
to sit in that empty house.

225
00:07:22,252 --> 00:07:24,330
And he took out his wallet and

226
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:26,269
showed me Loretta's picture.

227
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:29,051
And then he said something I've never

228
00:07:29,051 --> 00:07:29,708
forgotten.

229
00:07:29,888 --> 00:07:32,132
He said, you know why I stopped

230
00:07:32,132 --> 00:07:33,145
at your bench,

231
00:07:33,145 --> 00:07:33,580
ma'am?

232
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:36,240
Loretta would've had my hide if I'd

233
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,933
walked past a crying lady on Christmas

234
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:39,216
Eve.

235
00:07:39,396 --> 00:07:40,581
She always said,

236
00:07:40,581 --> 00:07:43,395
Jerome, you never know when you're the

237
00:07:43,395 --> 00:07:45,468
answer to somebody's prayer.

238
00:07:45,648 --> 00:07:47,868
I guess tonight you were the answer

239
00:07:47,868 --> 00:07:48,946
to mine, he said.

240
00:07:49,126 --> 00:07:51,483
I didn't want to sit alone either.

241
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:52,869
At six forty,

242
00:07:52,869 --> 00:07:56,139
the Illinois Highway Patrol pulled over a

243
00:07:56,139 --> 00:07:58,532
blue minivan with Ohio plates,

244
00:07:58,532 --> 00:08:01,084
a hundred and twelve miles west,

245
00:08:01,084 --> 00:08:03,955
because a trucker had radioed in its

246
00:08:03,955 --> 00:08:04,673
location.

247
00:08:04,853 --> 00:08:07,420
The trooper walked up to the window

248
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,447
and said, sir,

249
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:10,867
do you know where your mother is?

250
00:08:11,047 --> 00:08:12,894
And my son turned around,

251
00:08:12,894 --> 00:08:14,889
and looked in the back row,

252
00:08:14,889 --> 00:08:16,736
and pulled the coats off.

253
00:08:16,916 --> 00:08:18,449
Jenna screamed.

254
00:08:18,629 --> 00:08:21,284
The trooper said Mark went white as

255
00:08:21,284 --> 00:08:21,891
a sheet.

256
00:08:22,241 --> 00:08:25,445
Mark called Jerome's phone ten minutes later.

257
00:08:25,625 --> 00:08:27,756
He was crying so hard he could

258
00:08:27,756 --> 00:08:28,609
barely talk.

259
00:08:28,789 --> 00:08:30,405
He said, Mom,

260
00:08:30,405 --> 00:08:32,643
Mom, I'm so sorry.

261
00:08:32,823 --> 00:08:34,356
We're turning around.

262
00:08:34,536 --> 00:08:36,451
We'll be there in two hours.

263
00:08:36,631 --> 00:08:37,734
And I said,

264
00:08:37,734 --> 00:08:39,940
honey, take your time.

265
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,338
Drive slow in this snow.

266
00:08:42,518 --> 00:08:43,563
I'm fine.

267
00:08:43,743 --> 00:08:46,030
I'm having meatloaf with a friend.

268
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:47,785
And it was true,

269
00:08:47,785 --> 00:08:48,868
sweetheart.

270
00:08:49,048 --> 00:08:51,295
For the first time in a long

271
00:08:51,295 --> 00:08:54,424
time, somebody had really looked at me.

272
00:08:54,774 --> 00:08:57,360
When they pulled in at nine o'clock,

273
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,803
my son ran across that parking lot

274
00:08:59,803 --> 00:09:01,958
in the snow and grabbed me and

275
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,179
held on so tight.

276
00:09:03,359 --> 00:09:07,488
My grandkids, those teenagers with the headphones,

277
00:09:07,488 --> 00:09:08,479
were crying.

278
00:09:08,659 --> 00:09:09,971
All three of them.

279
00:09:10,151 --> 00:09:11,396
Jenna kept saying,

280
00:09:11,396 --> 00:09:13,541
I thought you were in the back.

281
00:09:13,721 --> 00:09:15,625
I thought you were sleeping.

282
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:16,929
And I said,

283
00:09:16,929 --> 00:09:18,359
I know, honey.

284
00:09:18,539 --> 00:09:19,445
I know.

285
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:21,204
But you didn't look.

286
00:09:21,384 --> 00:09:22,800
Nobody looked.

287
00:09:23,151 --> 00:09:25,840
And then I did something that surprised

288
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,529
everybody.

289
00:09:26,709 --> 00:09:27,786
I said, Mark,

290
00:09:27,786 --> 00:09:30,769
I'd like Jerome to come to Christmas

291
00:09:30,769 --> 00:09:32,177
dinner in Peoria.

292
00:09:32,357 --> 00:09:35,145
He's spending Christmas alone in a parking

293
00:09:35,145 --> 00:09:35,411
lot.

294
00:09:35,591 --> 00:09:37,530
Mark didn't even hesitate.

295
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:40,191
He shook Jerome's hand and said,

296
00:09:40,191 --> 00:09:42,284
sir, you're coming with us.

297
00:09:42,464 --> 00:09:44,520
And Jenna called her mother,

298
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,989
and her mother said,

299
00:09:45,989 --> 00:09:48,118
of course, set another place.

300
00:09:48,298 --> 00:09:51,377
And Jerome followed our minivan all the

301
00:09:51,377 --> 00:09:53,824
way to Illinois in his big rig.

302
00:09:54,175 --> 00:09:55,803
On Christmas morning,

303
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:58,361
Jerome sat by the tree in Jenna's

304
00:09:58,361 --> 00:09:59,989
parents' living room,

305
00:09:59,989 --> 00:10:01,539
with a paper hat on,

306
00:10:01,539 --> 00:10:04,020
watching the kids open presents.

307
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,692
And my oldest granddaughter,

308
00:10:06,692 --> 00:10:09,807
Emma, sixteen, sat down next to him

309
00:10:09,807 --> 00:10:11,944
and asked about Loretta.

310
00:10:12,124 --> 00:10:14,748
And then she asked about his daughter.

311
00:10:14,928 --> 00:10:16,925
And then she said the thing I'll

312
00:10:16,925 --> 00:10:17,737
never forget.

313
00:10:17,917 --> 00:10:19,601
She said, Mr.

314
00:10:19,781 --> 00:10:22,451
Jerome, have you called her today?

315
00:10:22,631 --> 00:10:24,036
It's Christmas.

316
00:10:24,386 --> 00:10:27,022
He hadn't called her in four years,

317
00:10:27,022 --> 00:10:27,474
honey.

318
00:10:27,654 --> 00:10:29,725
He said she wouldn't want to hear

319
00:10:29,725 --> 00:10:30,289
from him.

320
00:10:30,469 --> 00:10:32,729
And Emma held out her own phone

321
00:10:32,729 --> 00:10:34,916
and said, you don't know that.

322
00:10:35,096 --> 00:10:37,499
Loretta would want you to try.

323
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:40,226
You told Grandma you never know when

324
00:10:40,226 --> 00:10:42,985
you're the answer to somebody's prayer.

325
00:10:43,165 --> 00:10:46,571
Jerome looked at that sixteen-year-old for a

326
00:10:46,571 --> 00:10:47,345
long time.

327
00:10:47,525 --> 00:10:49,552
Then he went out on the porch

328
00:10:49,552 --> 00:10:50,601
with her phone.

329
00:10:50,952 --> 00:10:52,997
He was out there for an hour,

330
00:10:52,997 --> 00:10:53,773
sweetheart.

331
00:10:53,953 --> 00:10:55,413
When he came back in,

332
00:10:55,413 --> 00:10:56,664
his eyes were red,

333
00:10:56,664 --> 00:10:57,498
and he said,

334
00:10:57,498 --> 00:10:59,862
she's got two kids I've never met.

335
00:11:00,042 --> 00:11:01,946
She wants me to come for New

336
00:11:01,946 --> 00:11:02,422
Year's.

337
00:11:02,602 --> 00:11:05,273
Everybody in that living room cried.

338
00:11:05,453 --> 00:11:08,321
Jerome's been at his daughter's house every

339
00:11:08,321 --> 00:11:09,388
Christmas since.

340
00:11:09,568 --> 00:11:11,433
But every Christmas Eve,

341
00:11:11,433 --> 00:11:12,753
on his way there,

342
00:11:12,753 --> 00:11:15,239
he stops at that same truck stop

343
00:11:15,239 --> 00:11:16,093
in Indiana.

344
00:11:16,273 --> 00:11:17,771
And so do I.

345
00:11:18,121 --> 00:11:20,712
My family drives me there now,

346
00:11:20,712 --> 00:11:23,821
honey, every December twenty-fourth.

347
00:11:24,001 --> 00:11:26,109
We bring a big pan of meatloaf

348
00:11:26,109 --> 00:11:27,304
and a dozen pies,

349
00:11:27,304 --> 00:11:29,061
and we sit in that diner,

350
00:11:29,061 --> 00:11:31,731
and we feed any trucker who's spending

351
00:11:31,731 --> 00:11:33,277
Christmas on the road.

352
00:11:33,457 --> 00:11:35,687
Jerome tells the story.

353
00:11:35,867 --> 00:11:38,490
My grandkids hand out plates.

354
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:41,681
And nobody, nobody in that diner,

355
00:11:41,681 --> 00:11:44,417
sits alone by the ice machine.

356
00:11:44,597 --> 00:11:46,339
That's our tradition now.

357
00:11:46,689 --> 00:11:49,453
Here's what I want you to remember,

358
00:11:49,453 --> 00:11:50,322
sweetheart.

359
00:11:50,502 --> 00:11:53,335
Look up from your phone this Christmas.

360
00:11:53,515 --> 00:11:54,781
Count the heads.

361
00:11:54,961 --> 00:11:57,144
Look at the quiet old person in

362
00:11:57,144 --> 00:11:58,130
the back seat,

363
00:11:58,130 --> 00:12:00,243
and the stranger on the bench.

364
00:12:00,423 --> 00:12:02,941
You never know when you're the answer

365
00:12:02,941 --> 00:12:04,371
to somebody's prayer.

366
00:12:04,551 --> 00:12:06,457
Tell me in the comments,

367
00:12:06,457 --> 00:12:09,316
honey, have you ever been forgotten,

368
00:12:09,316 --> 00:12:10,031
or found?

369
00:12:10,211 --> 00:12:12,554
There are more of my family's stories

370
00:12:12,554 --> 00:12:14,771
in the playlist right there on your

371
00:12:14,771 --> 00:12:16,734
screen, and I'll see you in the

372
00:12:16,734 --> 00:12:17,304
next one.
